-- Per-query memory cap for the 'ingestor' ClickHouse user, covering both
-- the ingestor process and every detection/ job (they share this user --
-- see detection/config.py's own comment on why). Same category of change
-- as ingestor-user.sql.example: live instance state, stored under
-- /var/lib/clickhouse/access/ inside the clickhouse-data volume, so it
-- survives a plain container restart or recreate but is lost if that
-- volume is ever removed or recreated. If that happens, re-run this file
-- after re-running ingestor-user.sql.example.
--
-- Why this exists: 2026-09-14's ClickHouse OOM (docs/08-build-plan.md,
-- phase 4) was caused by an unbounded ad hoc query run with no per-query
-- limit -- max_memory_usage was 0 (unlimited) for every user, so a single
-- query could consume up to the whole server budget. This caps the
-- automated path. It does NOT cap the 'default' user, which is
-- XML-managed (/etc/clickhouse-server/users.d/default-user.xml, per
-- ingestor-user.sql.example's own note) and therefore read-only from SQL --
-- confirmed live: `ALTER USER default SETTINGS ...` fails with
-- ACCESS_STORAGE_READONLY. Capping 'default', and the server-wide
-- max_server_memory_usage ceiling, both require a docker-compose.yml
-- change (a mounted config.d override) -- proposed, not applied, in
-- docs/08-build-plan.md.
--
-- 1,000,000,000 bytes (~0.93 GiB): comfortably above any real query this
-- codebase runs today (every production query is address- or txid-scoped;
-- see docs/08-build-plan.md's OOM section for the per-query survey), and
-- comfortably below whatever the eventual server-wide ceiling turns out to
-- be, so a single runaway query fails on its own limit well before it
-- could threaten the server budget.
--
-- Proven 2026-09-22: the exact query shape that caused the OOM, rerun as
-- 'ingestor' with no query-level SETTINGS clause (relying purely on this
-- persisted user setting), failed cleanly:
--   Code: 241. DB::Exception: Query memory limit exceeded: would use
--   1.10 GiB (attempt to allocate chunk of 254.52 MiB bytes),
--   maximum: 953.67 MiB. (MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED)
-- No crash, no restart, nothing else affected.

ALTER USER ingestor SETTINGS max_memory_usage = 1000000000;
